# Scroll headed receipt. The local TLS fixture validates Scroll's distinct
# request line and three response metadata lines; this surface proves that a
# text/scroll body arrives through Turnstone's actor, route policy and native
# Nematic engine rather than degrading to gemtext.
settle 30
key escape
open scroll://127.0.0.1:19657/reading.scroll
settle 60
assert visible
act Toggle live content
settle 60
assert content-live
assert surface content
assert focused reading.scroll
capture 01_scroll_document
log smolweb Scroll browse receipt complete
